---

WebRTC carries glowcap between browsers over a direct DataChannel. A session's
bytes ride a
[WebRTC](https://www.w3.org/TR/webrtc/) DataChannel, encrypted with DTLS, with
no server on the byte path. Above the wire it is the same CapTP session.
What changes is how the channel comes up: a WebRTC peer has no
address to dial, so both ends arrange the connection through a capability they
can already reach.

# Dial

WebRTC is a signaling-mediated dial. TypeScript shows the managed connector
that ships today. Zig, Python, Rust, and Racket show the intended application
shape with an explicit `PLANNED` marker; each already exposes the lower-level
companion, but the managed adapter named by that marker has not landed yet.

